  "limitations": [
    "The original daily-profile first-screenshot timeout was not naturally reproduced; this is a rendering-liveness improvement based on an identified code-path gap, not proof that every capture timing failure is eliminated.",
    "The zero-before-navigation variant requests zero before navigating; its post-navigation viewport was already positive. Actual zero was separately verified in the after-navigation variants.",
    "The zero-frames variant explicitly primes animation frames, so first screenshot does not mean unpainted cold renderer in every scenario.",
    "The headed browser ran on an inactive Windows desktop with --no-startup-window and no --window-size. It does not prove behavior under every daily-profile feature combination.",
    "Existing pending Chrome read protection is unchanged. A screenshot or sync is not allowed to replay an uncertain action or bypass a pending renderer read."
  ]
